Subject: [PATCH 0171] santoni: retain coherent caches during ordinary WFI idle

Adapted from joranv1/ios-sailfish patch 0180-sailfish-idle-cache-pmap-aks.
Santoni uses coherent Cortex-A53 caches and plain WFI, not PSCI suspend or
cache/power collapse. The generic non-Apple idle hook cleans/invalidates by
set/way before every idle entry. Keep cache contents for ordinary WFI;
explicit startup handoff, DMA cache maintenance and shutdown are unchanged.
This is particularly important when driver polling has caused short sleeps.

--- a/osfmk/arm64/cpu.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/cpu.c
@@ -568,7 +568,11 @@
 #endif /* MONOTONIC */
 
 	if (wfi) {
-#if !defined(APPLE_ARM64_ARCH_FAMILY)
+#if !defined(APPLE_ARM64_ARCH_FAMILY) && !defined(SANTONI)
+		/* Santoni's plain WFI retains its coherent caches. There is no
+		 * PSCI suspend/power collapse here. Avoid whole-cache set/way
+		 * clean+invalidate on each idle entry, as ios-sailfish does. */
+		/* Other generic boards retain their existing cache-idle hook. */
 		platform_cache_idle_enter();
 #endif
 
